        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">The NordicTrack X24 is the steepest home treadmill we can confirm</strong>:
            -6% to 40%, a 4.25 CHP motor, a 400 lb rating and a 24-inch iFIT screen, at $4,299 on
            NordicTrack’s checkout page on 5 November 2026. Its steep end is for walking, not running,
            it needs a tall room, and most of the screen needs iFIT Pro at $39 a month.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For nearly everyone who wants a 40% incline trainer, the
            <a href="/best-nordictrack-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">NordicTrack X16</a>
            is the same machine for $600 less. Buy the X24 only if you will use the bigger screen every
            session, and do not pay list without checking promotions.
          </p>
